@meta
id: 21-08
title: Drill — search, edit, repeat
chapter: 21
type: drill
skills: macro-record, macro-count
par: 50
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: find next, type, find next, type
open: payment.spec.ts

@brief
Four tests, not adjacent, each needing `async` on the `it(` line and
`await` at the start of the line below. Record a macro that begins
with the search and ends without a `j`, then `99@a`.

@keys
| `/it(.*, () =>` | the next test that is still synchronous |
| `f(;` | past the first bracket to the second |
| `j^` | down, then to the first non-blank |

@hints
`qa`, the search, `f(;iasync ` `Esc`, `j^iawait ` `Esc`, `q`. Then
`99@a` and let the failed search stop it.
--
Do not press `j` at the end of the recording. The search at the start
is the step, and it works whether the next test is two lines away or
twenty.

@solution
    qa /it(.*, () => <Enter> f(; iasync  <Esc> j^ iawait  <Esc> q   99@a   :wq<Enter>

Forty-four keystrokes. The habit being drilled: when the targets are
scattered, the first key in the recording is `/`.

@start payment.spec.ts
describe('PaymentService', () => {
  it('refunds a paid order', () => {
    service.refund('ord_101');
    expect(http.post).toHaveBeenCalledWith('/refunds', { orderId: 'ord_101' });
  });

  it('throws when the gateway rejects', () => {
    service.refund('ord_102');
    expect(http.post).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
  });

  describe('retries', () => {
    it('retries once on a timeout', () => {
      service.refund('ord_103');
      expect(http.post).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);
    });

    it('gives up after the second timeout', () => {
      service.refund('ord_104');
      expect(http.post).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);
    });
  });
});

@expected payment.spec.ts
describe('PaymentService', () => {
  it('refunds a paid order', async () => {
    await service.refund('ord_101');
    expect(http.post).toHaveBeenCalledWith('/refunds', { orderId: 'ord_101' });
  });

  it('throws when the gateway rejects', async () => {
    await service.refund('ord_102');
    expect(http.post).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
  });

  describe('retries', () => {
    it('retries once on a timeout', async () => {
      await service.refund('ord_103');
      expect(http.post).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);
    });

    it('gives up after the second timeout', async () => {
      await service.refund('ord_104');
      expect(http.post).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);
    });
  });
});
